# hpcworker framework 30 and 31: job submit --placement and job place's candidates and cards for the site wayne (lib/jobs.sh reads it).
# A candidate is a partition with the QoS it takes, in the order a tie goes: never preempted first. reqp takes
# requeue, which the gpu, primary, secondary and debug QoS preempt (preempt/qos), so a job placed there is
# requeued and resumes from its last checkpoint. express belongs to the hardware investors and is never a
# candidate. Framework 31 races the candidates of one QoS together and submits a job to all of them at once.
# MAX, where given, is the most of this account's jobs that QoS may hold at once: the debug QoS allows one user
# 4 cores and 2 submitted jobs (sacctmgr, 2026-11-04), so one runner job, and it takes reqp, prip and secp.
# The runner class is tools/grid_runner.sh's autoscaler (job place --class runner): CI runner jobs, which
# nothing resumes, so a QoS never preempted comes first.
#   candidate CLASS PARTITION QOS PREEMPTABLE [MAX]
candidate gpu galhp gpu no
candidate gpu gmsap gpu no
candidate gpu gvohp gpu no
candidate gpu reqp requeue yes
candidate cpu secp secondary no
candidate cpu prip primary no
candidate cpu reqp requeue yes
candidate runner reqp debug no 1
candidate runner prip debug no 1
candidate runner secp debug no 1
candidate runner prip primary no
candidate runner secp secondary no
candidate runner reqp requeue yes
# Framework 35: a constraint is a node feature (sinfo's %f, scontrol's AvailableFeatures) every job of the class
# asks for, in the race's sbatch --test-only and in the options job place prints, so a partition with no such node
# is refused and drops out of the race. Runner jobs ask for avx2: SchwingNet's required check, a serial unittest
# run, took 25 to 56 minutes on secp's asx nodes (4-socket AMD Opterons, features asx,amd,avx,10e, no avx2) and
# 8 to 14 on mdt, sfx and GitHub's machines on 5 November 2026, and ran into its 55-minute limit on asx1; secp's
# only nodes in service are asx, so the debug QoS's one runner job landed there nearly every time.
#   constraint CLASS FEATURE
constraint runner avx2
# A card is a GPU type as sinfo's GRES column names it, its memory in GB and its architecture; one with a
# partition after it holds there alone (tesla is a V100 on gvohp and a K20X or older elsewhere).
#   card GRES_TYPE MEMORY_GB ARCH [PARTITION]
card nvidia_h200 141 hopper
card nvidia_l40s 48 ada
card nvidia_a30 24 ampere
card nvidia_a30_2g.12gb 12 ampere
card nvidia_a100_80gb_pcie_1g.10gb 10 ampere
card nvidia_rtx_pro_4500_blackwell 32 blackwell
card nvidia_rtx_pro_4000_blackwell 24 blackwell
card geforce 11 turing
card tesla 16 volta gvohp
card tesla 6 kepler
